01:01:45,000 --> 01:01:51,000
Rudy is a 1993 American biographical sports film directed by David Anspaugh.

14
01:06:30,000 --> 01:06:36,000
It is an account of the life of Daniel "Rudy" Ruettiger, who harbored dreams of playing
football at the University of Notre Dame despite significant obstacles.

15
01:11:15,000 --> 01:11:21,000
It was the first film that the Notre Dame administration allowed to be
shot on campus since Knute Rockne, All American in 1940.

16
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
In 2005, Rudy was named one of the best 25 sports movies of the previous 25 years in two
polls by ESPN (#24 by a panel of sports experts, and #4 by ESPN.com users).

17
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:51,000
It was ranked the 54th-most inspiring film of all time in the
American Film Institute's "100 Years" series.

18
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film premiered at the Toronto International Film Festival on September 18, 1993, and
was released in the United States on October 13, 1993, by TriStar Pictures.

